#: inc/panel.php:1519
msgid "Enable WordPress Sitemap"
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:1526
msgid "Generates <code>/wp-sitemap.xml</code> with sub-sitemaps for posts, pages, taxonomies and authors (WP 5.5+ native). Disable only if you use a third-party SEO plugin (Yoast, RankMath) that provides its own sitemap."
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:1531
msgid "Include Authors in Sitemap"
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:1538
msgid "Adds <code>/wp-sitemap-users-1.xml</code> with author archive URLs. Useful for multi-author blogs. <strong>Leave off for solo blogs</strong> — the author archive duplicates the home page and creates near-duplicate content for crawlers."
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:1543
msgid "Include Custom Post Types in Sitemap"
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:1550
msgid "Includes any public Custom Post Types registered by the theme or plugins (alongside the standard <code>post</code> and <code>page</code>). Turn off if you have CPTs you don't want indexed (e.g. portfolio items used only as widgets)."
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:1555
msgid "IndexNow"
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:1558
msgid "Enable IndexNow"
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:1565
msgid "Notifies Bing, Yandex and other participating engines the moment a post or page is published, updated or unpublished — push indexing in minutes instead of waiting for the crawler. One ping is shared between all participating engines. <strong>Google does not join IndexNow</strong>, so keep the sitemap on. The key file is served automatically at <code>/{key}.txt</code> — nothing to upload."
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:1570
msgid "IndexNow Key"
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:1577
msgid "auto-generated on save when empty"
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:1582
msgid "robots.txt"
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:1585
msgid "Custom robots.txt"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s = the site's sitemap URL like https://site.com/wp-sitemap.xml — appears inside a <pre> code block showing the WP default robots.txt
#: inc/panel.php:1594
#, php-format
msgid "Override the WordPress default <code>/robots.txt</code> entirely. Leave empty to keep the WP-generated content. When filled, this <strong>replaces</strong> the output completely — you must include all directives you want crawlers to see.<br><br><strong>WP defaults (what you are overriding):</strong><pre class=\"rd-robots-defaults\">User-agent: *%1$sDisallow: /wp-admin/%1$sAllow: /wp-admin/admin-ajax.php%1$s%1$sSitemap: %2$s</pre>Copy any defaults you want to keep into your custom output. Common additions: block LLM scrapers (<code>GPTBot</code>, <code>ClaudeBot</code>, <code>CCBot</code>), block search/pagination URLs, declare multiple sitemaps."
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:1606
msgid "Ads — Global Script"
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:1609
msgid "Global Ad Script"
